{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789828198,"nonce":"Go4+9Q7YLYLk2rba+FMkHvK7MGs=","message":"Ash reload landed: ash 12e6a40 (on ash main) and caribou 95380b8c190aae030585999b817726acbe958dff.\n\nAsh's hot reload was an LLVM-tier feature (`--hot-reload` forced `--jit-tier=llvm`; `do_reload` recompiled changed bodies with LLVM), and caribou builds ash without LLVM. The ash change makes it work on the interpreter + Cranelift ladder: `do_reload` without the `llvm` feature diffs the bodies by hash, writes the stub sentinel (`findex + 1`) back into each changed body's `functions_ptrs` slot so compiled callers' guarded calls re-enter the interpreter (which walks the new program after `apply_reload`), does the same for every compiled body whose cached AIR has an inline site naming a changed callee (`air_pipeline::inline_dependents`, read before the cache is dropped), flushes the vtables, and returns the new program; the tiers promote again from it. `stage_reload()` is the host's entry: it reads the file, diffs, and refuses a program that cannot replace the running one in place (layout, globals count, added/removed functions, or a findex whose `Type.name` moved), else stages the decoded program and sets the pending flag. `HLInterpreter::enable_reload(path, resolver)` registers the context without tiers (extracted from `enable_tiered`, which still calls it under `hot_reload`), and `poll_reload` applies a pending reload for a host entering from outside.\n\ncaribou: `caribou_ash::Options::reload` (default on; off for `load_bytes` and the compare runner), `Runtime::reload` = `stage_reload`, `Program::publish` records the `.hl` under the program's name so the watch covers it, `Session::call` polls before dispatch, `Session::Options::reload` (benches set it off: under reload ash lowers the walker's AIR without inlining and enters no interpreted loop by OSR, ash's own trade). Test: crates/caribou-interop/tests/reload_haxe.rs (fixture reload.hl; `answer` compiled by the tier, then the bytecode's constant edited and re-encoded with `bytecode_encode` — no haxe at test time; 42 -\u003e 52 through the compiled slot, warm re-promotes; a rebuild with another globals count is refused and names the change).\n\nNot covered: a rebuild that changes the program's shape (a method added or removed shifts findexes; Ash refuses it, the program restarts), the LLVM path under caribou (untouched), field-default patches for live objects (`apply_field_patches` walks the heap through `hlp_gc_walk_heap`; not called on the sentinel path, since under the seam the heap is the core's). Still open here: the quiescent point with worker worlds; TypeDesc-level epochs if ever needed.","files":null}]}